-- title:
--   Extending anemic Hecke points with prescribed U_q-eigenvalues
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$ be an integer and let $S_0 \subseteq S$ be finite sets of natural numbers such that every prime dividing $N$ lies in $S$. For a set $\Sigma$ of naturals write $\mathbb{T}^{\Sigma}(N)$ for [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 Σ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to the primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin \Sigma$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to the primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin \Sigma$; since $S_0 \subseteq S$ one has $\mathbb{T}^{S}(N) \le \mathbb{T}^{S_0}(N)$, and [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.U hq hqN hqS`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L80) denotes the element of $\mathbb{T}^{\Sigma}(N)$ given by `heckeULin` at a prime $q \mid N$, $q \notin \Sigma$. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero, adically complete for its maximal ideal and with finite residue field, and let $\chi : \mathbb{T}^{S}(N) \to \mathcal{O}'$ be a ring homomorphism. Then there is a type $\mathcal{O}''$ carrying the structure of a discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero, adically complete for its maximal ideal and with finite residue field, together with an $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra structure making $\mathcal{O}''$ a finite $\mathcal{O}'$-module with $\mathcal{O}' \to \mathcal{O}''$ a local and injective homomorphism, and a ring homomorphism $\chi' : \mathbb{T}^{S_0}(N) \to \mathcal{O}''$ such that: $\chi'$ restricted along the inclusion $\mathbb{T}^{S}(N) \hookrightarrow \mathbb{T}^{S_0}(N)$ equals $\chi$ followed by $\mathcal{O}' \to \mathcal{O}''$; $\chi'(U_q) = 0$ for every prime $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S_0$ and $q^2 \mid N$; and $\chi'(U_q)$ divides $q$ in $\mathcal{O}''$ for every prime $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S_0$ and $q^2 \nmid N$.
--
--   This is the passage from a system of Hecke eigenvalues away from $S$ to a point of the fuller Hecke algebra away from $S_0$ realised by an oldform of level $N$, as in Darmon–Diamond–Taylor §4.2 (the eigenform $g$ constructed before Lemma 4.6), with the $U_q$-eigenvalue vanishing at primes with $q^2 \mid N$ and dividing $q$ at primes exactly dividing $N$. It is the automorphic input to the comparison between the anemic and the full local Hecke algebras, and is used by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_of_subset_of_forall_prime_mem_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_of_subset_of_forall_prime_mem_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq).
